1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,176
QuakeSense asks a practical question: when does local AI leadership actually improve earthquake evacuation?

2
00:00:07,176 --> 00:00:17,426
We connect local language-model leaders, millions of resident agents, real road networks, and an inspectable WebGIS in one working system.

3
00:00:18,076 --> 00:00:21,647
The loop begins with real city state.

4
00:00:21,647 --> 00:00:27,767
A leader observes local hazards, shelter pressure, road access, and resident belief.

5
00:00:27,767 --> 00:00:36,948
It reasons with compact memory, calls validated tools, changes the simulation, and exposes the result in the WebGIS.

6
00:00:37,598 --> 00:00:43,669
Every ten minutes, scheduled jurisdiction leaders observe, reason, plan, use tools, and execute.

7
00:00:43,669 --> 00:00:55,344
Their broadcasts change what residents know and where they move, so the next resident step responds to the decision instead of replaying a fixed animation.

8
00:00:55,994 --> 00:00:59,572
At the microscopic level, roles matter.

9
00:00:59,572 --> 00:01:11,496
Commanders broadcast, informed residents guide, uninformed residents follow, volunteers assist elderly people and children, and responders manage arrivals at shelters.

10
00:01:12,146 --> 00:01:15,740
Four implemented rules create the city process.

11
00:01:15,740 --> 00:01:28,577
Departure delays are distributed, boundary flow is limited by width and pedestrian specific flow, destinations require remaining shelter capacity, and every time step conserves population.

12
00:01:29,227 --> 00:01:33,171
This Naples run shows the resident layer in motion.

13
00:01:33,171 --> 00:01:40,622
Orange agents are still travelling, green agents have reached shelter, and the road hierarchy constrains every route.

14
00:01:40,622 --> 00:01:46,319
The model represents individual movement, not an aggregate flow painted onto a map.

15
00:01:46,969 --> 00:01:51,213
Before leadership is evaluated, QuakeSense diagnoses physical access.

16
00:01:51,213 --> 00:01:57,048
Wellington, Kathmandu, Los Angeles, and Naples begin with high static access.

17
00:01:57,048 --> 00:02:05,005
Mandalay and L Aquila are lower, while Noto exposes a severe capacity and network bottleneck.

18
00:02:05,655 --> 00:02:11,636
At fifteen minutes, leadership improves early safety in five of seven overseas cities.

19
00:02:11,636 --> 00:02:14,856
The effect is measurable but not universal.

20
00:02:14,856 --> 00:02:21,757
Noto and L Aquila decline because information cannot create missing road throughput or shelter capacity.

21
00:02:22,407 --> 00:02:26,215
The same policy can help early and harm later.

22
00:02:26,215 --> 00:02:30,445
Faster guidance may concentrate demand at the same constrained destinations.

23
00:02:30,445 --> 00:02:39,753
In Noto, the late effect reverses sharply, which is exactly why the system reports limits rather than claiming that AI always wins.

24
00:02:40,403 --> 00:02:55,090
Los Angeles provides the strongest large-city portfolio case: six point two eight million residents represented as agents across more than two hundred thirty thousand road blocks, with full-population movement visible on the real network.

25
00:02:55,740 --> 00:02:58,610
Noto, Japan provides the stress case.

26
00:02:58,610 --> 00:03:07,222
Its dispersed settlement pattern, limited road redundancy, and constrained shelter structure make access difficult even with better information.

27
00:03:07,222 --> 00:03:13,441
This is a demanding test of both the simulator and the leadership hypothesis.

28
00:03:14,091 --> 00:03:19,159
All language-model inference runs locally on AMD Radeon through ROCm.

29
00:03:19,159 --> 00:03:28,281
The measured run uses a quantized Qwen model, concurrent inference slots, grammar-constrained decisions, and an explicit VRAM budget.

30
00:03:28,281 --> 00:03:32,842
Validated tool calls are applied back into the simulation.

31
00:03:33,492 --> 00:03:38,681
The stack is tuned for shared throughput and decision validity.

32
00:03:38,681 --> 00:03:51,653
Full GPU offload, four-bit quantization, continuous batching, compact context, and constrained JSON keep the language model and resident simulator sharing one Radeon without losing inspectability.

33
00:03:52,303 --> 00:03:56,891
The evidence is strongest when its limits are explicit.

34
00:03:56,891 --> 00:04:03,008
The agent mechanism, real road networks, and measured local inference are established.

35
00:04:03,008 --> 00:04:10,144
Repeated seeds, matched baselines, calibration, and further controlled comparisons remain the next evidence steps.

36
00:04:10,794 --> 00:04:19,748
The research contribution is an auditable scenario laboratory linking individual behavior, physical capacity, information, and city-scale outcomes.

37
00:04:19,748 --> 00:04:28,175
It supports privacy-preserving counterfactual analysis, but it is not a forecast or an official evacuation plan.

38
00:04:28,825 --> 00:04:38,618
We gratefully acknowledge AMD for cloud computing resources that supported large-scale data preparation, multi-city simulation, rendering, and validation.

39
00:04:38,618 --> 00:04:45,147
This acknowledgment does not imply AMD endorsement of the methods or conclusions.
